Spec: Feature Issue 30 - Fix Mock Auth and Admin RBAC

Purpose:
  Remove the hardcoded "admin" username from audit logs and ensure in-memory administrators from config.json are correctly recognized by the RBAC API.

Platform: Rust/Linux

References:
  ../../../core-layer.sdd

Owns:
  ./**

Can modify:
  /mitm_http-server/src/handlers/admin.rs
  /mitm_http-server/src/handlers/rbac.rs

Must:
  Extract the actual authenticated username from `Extension<AuthResponse>` in `admin.rs` handlers instead of hardcoding "admin".
  Check `config.admins` in `handle_get_os_user_roles` before querying the database, returning `["ADMIN"]` if the user is a statically configured admin.
  Decode `MASTER_KEY` via base64 in `mitm_scheduler-server/src/main.rs` if length is 44, exactly as done in IAM server.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Replace hardcoded "admin" strings with `auth.username` in `mitm_http-server/src/handlers/admin.rs`.
  [x] #2 Add fallback to `state.config.admins` in `mitm_http-server/src/handlers/rbac.rs`.
  [x] #3 Decode `MASTER_KEY` via base64 in `mitm_scheduler-server/src/main.rs`.
